    "body": "## Description\n\nReject non-inline image sources before local base64 decoding with a clear error for both\nOpenAI-compatible proxy requests and direct `ArealOpenAI` calls. Clarify the inline-only\ncontract in docstrings and validation messages while preserving URL forwarding for\ntokenizer-only clients.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nFixes #1770\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [x] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the\n  [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [x] Documentation updated (function docstrings and validation messages; no docs site\n  changes)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [x] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n## Additional Context\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/experimental/openai/test_vlm_trajectory.py -q`: **28 passed**.\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: **passed**.\n\nTests cover valid inline PNG/JPEG images, rejection of unsupported sources before\ndecoding, invalid image data, and unchanged HTTP(S) URL extraction.\n\nGPU/distributed and live proxy integration tests were not run in this CPU test\nenvironment. No docs site build was needed for docstring-only documentation changes.\n",
